 {
  "id": "g-modals",
  "level": "B1",
  "title_fr": "Les verbes modaux (can, must, should, may)",
  "rule_fr": [
   "Les modaux sont suivis de l'infinitif sans « to » et ne prennent jamais de -s à he, she, it.",
   "can / could : capacité, permission. I can swim.",
   "must : obligation forte ou forte probabilité. You must wear a seatbelt. He must be tired.",
   "should : conseil. You should rest.",
   "may / might : possibilité. It may rain.",
   "Négation : cannot (can't), mustn't (interdit), shouldn't.",
   "Attention : mustn't = interdit ; don't have to = pas obligé."
  ],
  "formula": [
   {
    "label": "Sujet",
    "text": "sujet",
    "color": "subject",
    "row": 0
   },
   {
    "label": "Auxiliaire",
    "text": "can / must / should / may",
    "color": "aux",
    "row": 0
   },
